# Line endings, once, for every platform.
#
# Without this file git applies the contributor's core.autocrlf, so a Windows
# checkout turns every text file into CRLF. That is invisible for compilers and
# invisible in `git status` (git compares after normalising), but the TUI's
# acceptance frames are compared byte-for-byte — so on Windows the golden test
# failed while the file looked unchanged. Normalise on the way in, hand every
# platform the same bytes.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The golden frames are an exact contract: never converted, on any machine.
tui-go/app/testdata/golden/*.txt text eol=lf

# Binaries are never text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.so binary
*.dylib binary
*.pyc binary
*.zip binary
